WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.137
Weights and hidden states are easy to confuse, so keep them separate.

00:00:04.137 --> 00:00:06.872
Weights are learned model parameters.

00:00:06.872 --> 00:00:10.382
Training changes them, and the checkpoint stores them.

00:00:10.382 --> 00:00:15.172
During ordinary inference, those weights normally stay fixed.

00:00:15.172 --> 00:00:20.797
Hidden states are temporary vectors created while the current prompt moves through the model.

00:00:20.797 --> 00:00:26.720
They are recomputed for every new input and change from one Transformer layer to the next.

00:00:27.524 --> 00:00:31.471
A useful summary is: training learns the weights.

00:00:31.471 --> 00:00:36.989
Inference uses those fixed weights to compute new hidden states for the current prompt.
